const newContent={home:[['Find your starting point.','The visible change is a useful beginning. Choose the detail that best describes your space and explore what to ask next.',['Standing water|Share the source, room layout and access to the affected area.','A damp finish|Describe the material, visible marks and when you noticed them.','A damaged surface|Discuss retained finishes, preparation and matching the repair.'],'r7-1'],['Room for better decisions.','A well-prepared enquiry brings the important details together. Keep observations separate from assumptions and let a property-specific assessment fill the gaps.',['What you can see|Describe the change in your own words.','What you know|Include the timing and known point of entry.','What matters|Explain the materials you hope to keep.','What to ask|Request the scope, exclusions and next steps.'],'r7-2'],['Different rooms. Connected stories.','Explore the room in its wider setting. A threshold, a shared wall or a change in floor level can connect one observation to another.',['Living areas|Include adjoining rooms and everyday use.','Thresholds|Describe where the finish or level changes.','Hidden layers|Ask what further access may be needed.'],'r7-3'],['A clearer brief.','Move from a first observation to a useful conversation. Bring together the room, the event and the questions you want answered.',['The observation|Note visible changes without guessing what lies behind them.','The context|Describe the timing, source if known and connected areas.','The conversation|Ask how findings, costs and responsibilities will be explained.'],'r7-4'],['Services that connect.','Understand where each service belongs. Your chosen provider can explain how the stages overlap in your property.',['Water extraction|Standing water removal begins with an assessment of the source, affected area and access. Ask what is included in removal and what happens afterwards.','Structural drying|Discuss moisture retained in the construction, the proposed equipment and how progress will be recorded. Agree access and review arrangements.','Damage restoration|Bring preparation, retained materials and finish matching into the written scope. Review samples and clarify the checks at handover.'],'r7-5']],extract:[['The route water takes.','A practical description starts with the setting. Include changes in level, connected rooms and the known point of entry.',['The entry point|State what is known and what still needs investigation.','The affected area|Describe standing water and connected spaces.','The access route|Include stairs, doors and restrictions on equipment access.'],'r7-6'],['Protect the wider space.','Discuss how unaffected rooms and belongings will be considered during the proposed work. Get responsibilities into the written scope.',['Floors and thresholds|Ask how access routes will be protected.','Furniture and contents|Clarify what is moved and by whom.','Shared spaces|Discuss access with anyone who uses the entrance.','After removal|Confirm which observations inform the next stage.'],'service-15'],['A considered setup.','Equipment decisions belong to the property assessment. Explain the layout and ask how the proposed approach suits the room.',['Access|Include narrow openings and changes in level.','Surfaces|Describe finishes in contact with the water.','Follow-up|Ask what is checked once visible water is removed.'],'r7-7'],['From removal to review.','Follow the questions that connect extraction with the next assessment. Keep a clear record of what was found and what remains uncertain.',['Prepare|Share the room layout and known timing before the visit.','Discuss|Ask what removal includes and how the space is protected.','Review|Request findings and recommendations for retained moisture.'],'service-16'],['Before you agree.','A useful quotation describes the work as clearly as the price. Use these points to prepare your next conversation.',['Included work|Equipment, labour, access and the areas covered.','Possible changes|How additional work will be explained and agreed.','Completion record|What findings and recommendations you will receive.'],'service-18']],dry:[['A view beneath the finish.','Construction gives moisture observations their meaning. Share known layers and discuss what can be checked without opening a surface.',['Timber|Ask how readings relate to the material and finish.','Plaster|Describe staining, movement and adjoining surfaces.','Masonry|Discuss construction and the method used to assess it.'],'r7-8'],['Make room for the plan.','A drying proposal affects the way a room is used. Discuss practical arrangements before agreeing equipment and visits.',['Equipment position|Understand the proposed layout.','Room access|Clarify where access must remain clear.','Repeat visits|Ask how checks are arranged and recorded.','Plan changes|Agree how adjustments will be communicated.'],'service-8'],['The detail in a reading.','One value needs context. Ask about the instrument, location, material and limitations before drawing conclusions.',['The method|Understand what the selected measurement can show.','The location|Connect each reading to the room and construction.','The pattern|Discuss changes over time and adjacent areas.'],'r7-9'],['Keep progress in view.','A shared record helps make the plan understandable. Ask how repeat observations support changes to the setup and the move towards repair.',['Baseline|Request the initial findings and the areas checked.','Review|Ask what has changed and whether further checks are needed.','Next stage|Clarify the evidence used to recommend finishing work.'],'editorial-17'],['Questions for each visit.','Bring the room’s use, materials and previous findings into the review. You do not need to interpret readings by yourself.',['What changed?|Ask for an explanation of new observations.','What stays in place?|Clarify the equipment and access arrangements.','What happens next?|Agree the next review and the information you will receive.'],'extra-restore-2']],restore:[['A finish worth considering.','A repaired area is part of the whole room. Bring existing materials, light and transitions into the conversation before selecting a finish.',['Keep|Ask which sound materials can remain.','Prepare|Clarify what happens beneath the new finish.','Connect|Consider the edges where old and new meet.'],'r7-10'],['Details make the room.','A small sample can make a broad description more useful. Review colour and texture in the space where the repair will be seen.',['Colour|Consider the room’s natural and artificial light.','Texture|Compare the surface from more than one angle.','Junctions|Include skirtings, reveals and thresholds.','Care|Ask for relevant maintenance information.'],'extra-restore-1'],['Preparation with purpose.','Discuss the condition of the underlying surface and what is included before a new finish is applied. Agree which areas are retained and which are repaired.',['Surface condition|Ask how readiness for repair is assessed.','Material choice|Discuss suitable options for the existing construction.','Final appearance|Clarify the limits of matching old and new.'],'r7-11'],['From sample to finish.','Use the conversation to connect appearance with the written scope. Confirm preparation, application and handover details directly with your provider.',['Explore|Share the finishes you value and the result you hope for.','Compare|Review samples alongside the materials that remain.','Confirm|Agree the selected finish and any matching limitations.'],'extra-restore-3'],['A thoughtful handover.','Bring the agreed details back into view at the end of the work. Ask how finishing items, care information and remaining questions will be recorded.',['Review the scope|Compare the completed areas with the agreed work.','Discuss the details|Raise junctions, edges and any finishing items.','Keep the record|Retain the scope, finish information and correspondence.'],'r7-12']]};
function newSections(key){const layouts=key==='home'?['directory','checker','fold','story','service-list']:key==='extract'?['directory','tiles','offset','story','checklist']:key==='dry'?['offset','checker','directory','story','checklist']:['directory','tiles','offset','story','checklist'];return newContent[key].map((d,n)=>{const [givenTitle,copy,items,photo]=d,ls=items.map(x=>x.split('|')),id=`${key}-detail-${n+1}`,kind=layouts[n];const title=({'home-detail-1':'A fresh start.','home-detail-2':'Clear choices.','extract-detail-1':'Water pathways.','extract-detail-2':'Space protected.','dry-detail-2':'Plan the space.','dry-detail-3':'Read the detail.','restore-detail-1':'Finish matters.','restore-detail-2':'Room for detail.'})[id]||givenTitle;const stripIds=['home-detail-1','home-detail-2','extract-detail-1','extract-detail-2','dry-detail-2','dry-detail-3','restore-detail-1','restore-detail-2'];const strip=stripIds.indexOf(id);const intro=`<div class="n-intro"><h2>${title}</h2><p>${copy}</p>${strip>=0?`<figure class="n-flood-strip">${img('r8-strip-'+strip,'Water across the floor of a residential interior')}</figure>`:''}</div>`,photoHtml=img(photo,title);let content='';if(kind==='directory')content=`<div class="n-directory">${intro}<div class="n-directory-list">${ls.map(([t,p],i)=>`<a href="${key==='home'?services[i].id+'.html':'contact.html?service='+services.find(s=>s.key===key).id}"><div><h3>${t}</h3><p>${p}</p></div><span class="n-row-photo">${photoHtml}</span>${I(['waves','scan-line','layers'][i])}</a>`).join('')}</div></div>`;if(kind==='checker'||kind==='tiles')content=`<div class="n-checker-layout ${kind==='tiles'?'reverse':''}">${intro}<div class="n-checker" data-mosaic>${ls.map(([t,p],i)=>`<article tabindex="0" class="n-tile tile-${i}">${i===0?photoHtml:I(['house','scan-line','layers','clipboard-check'][i])}<div><h3>${t}</h3><p>${p}</p></div></article>`).join('')}</div></div>`;if(kind==='fold')content=`${intro}<div class="n-fold" data-fold>${ls.map(([t,p],i)=>`<button class="${i===0?'active':''}" aria-expanded="${i===0}">${img(i===0?photo:i===1?'editorial-18':'service-18',t)}<span><strong>${t}</strong><small>${p}</small></span>${I(['house','door-open','layers'][i])}</button>`).join('')}</div>`;if(kind==='offset')content=`<div class="n-offset"><figure>${photoHtml}<figcaption>${I('scan-line')} The whole room matters.</figcaption></figure><div>${intro}<div class="n-feature-list">${ls.map(([t,p],i)=>`<article tabindex="0">${I(['layers','scan-line','clipboard-check'][i])}<div><h3>${t}</h3><p>${p}</p></div></article>`).join('')}</div></div></div>`;if(kind==='story')content=`<div class="n-story"><div class="n-story-banner">${photoHtml}${intro}</div><div class="n-story-body" data-story><div class="n-story-nav" role="tablist" aria-label="${title}">${ls.map(([t],i)=>`<button role="tab" id="${id}-tab-${i}" aria-controls="${id}-panel-${i}" aria-selected="${i===0}">${t}</button>`).join('')}</div>${ls.map(([t,p],i)=>`<div class="n-story-panel" role="tabpanel" id="${id}-panel-${i}" aria-labelledby="${id}-tab-${i}" ${i?'hidden':''}><h3>${t}, with context.</h3><p>${p} ${copy}</p><a class="n-link" href="contact.html">Bring this into your enquiry</a></div>`).join('')}</div></div>`;if(kind==='service-list')content=`${intro}<div class="n-services">${ls.map(([t,p],i)=>`<details ${i===0?'open':''}><summary>${I(services[i].icon)}<h3>${t}</h3><span>${I('plus')}</span></summary><div class="n-service-body"><div><p>${p}</p>${tickItems(i===0?['Source and extent','Equipment access','What follows removal']:i===1?['Affected construction','Monitoring and records','Criteria for the next stage']:['Preparation and repair','Samples and transitions','A clear handover'])}${btn(services[i].id+'.html','Explore the service','outline')}</div>${img(i===0?photo:i===1?'extra-restore-2':'r7-12',t)}</div></details>`).join('')}</div>`;if(kind==='checklist')content=`<div class="n-checklist">${intro}<div class="n-ready"><span class="n-ready-value"><b data-ready-number>30</b><small>%</small></span><p>Your enquiry checklist</p><div class="n-ready-track"><span></span></div><p class="n-ready-caption">A starting outline is ready. Add these two details to complete your brief.</p><label><input type="checkbox" data-ready> I can describe the affected room.</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-ready> I have questions for a provider.</label></div><div class="n-checklist-notes">${ls.map(([t,p])=>`<article><h3>${t}</h3><p>${p}</p></article>`).join('')}</div></div>`;return section(id,`new-section n-${kind}-section`,content)})}
